---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import BuildUpLink from "../../components/UnderTheHood/BuildUpLink.astro"
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro"
import Example from "../../components/Example/index"
import FieldSizingCompare from "../../components/Blog/FieldSizingCompare.astro"
import AutoFit from "../../component-examples/textarea/AutoFit.astro"
---

<TechniquePost slug="textarea-field-sizing">
  <section id="the-problem">
    <h2>The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> is as tall as its <code>rows</code> attribute
      says, no matter what's in it. Short notes leave empty space, long ones scroll
      inside a tiny box.
    </p>
    <p>
      The usual fix is JavaScript that listens to <code>input</code>, resets the
      height and sets it to <code>scrollHeight</code> on every keystroke. Not anymore.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="the-trick">
    <h2>The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>field-sizing: content</code> sizes the textarea to its text: it grows
        as you type and shrinks as you delete
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>lh</code> is one line of the textarea's own text, so limits read as
        line counts
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>min-block-size</code> keeps at least three lines, <code
          >max-block-size</code
        > caps it at 20, then it scrolls
      </li>
      <li><code>resize: block</code> still lets the user drag it taller</li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="css"
      code={`textarea {
  block-size: auto;
  field-sizing: content;
  max-block-size: var(--_max-block-size, 20lh);
  min-block-size: calc(var(--_field-padding-block-fit) * 2 + 3lh);
  resize: block;
}`}
    />
  </section>

  <section id="try-it">
    <h2>Try it</h2>
    <p>
      Type in either box, both get the same text. Then move the line limits.
    </p>
    <Example wide showCode={false}>
      <FieldSizingCompare />
    </Example>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>content</code> grows a line at a time until the max, then scrolls. Delete
        text and it shrinks back to the min
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>fixed</code> is the default: the box stays at its <code>rows</code
        > and scrolls inside
      </li>
      <li>
        The limits are in <code>lh</code>, so they read as line counts whatever
        the font size
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Type a few lines. It grows with them, and shrinks when you delete.</p>
    <Example showCode={false}>
      <AutoFit />
    </Example>
    <BuildUpLink />
  </section>

  <section id="fallback">
    <h2>Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Browsers without <code>field-sizing</code> ignore it, and the textarea keeps
        its <code>rows</code> height, never less than three lines
      </li>
      <li>Long text scrolls and the resize handle still works</li>
      <li>Nothing breaks, it just doesn't grow</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
